# ESP32-S3 Wearable WebSocket Architecture Migration Plan

This plan documents the upcoming architectural migration for the **Wearable ESP32-S3 Firmware Setup Mode**, transitioning from `ESPAsyncWebServer` HTTP registration handling to a dedicated **WebSocket Server Architecture (`WebSocketsServer` on port 81)**, matching the dark slate design system rules.

> [!NOTE]
> All current progress, aesthetic redesigns, pin markers, profile drawers, receiver captive portal updates, and zero-emoji design rules have been saved and verified (0 build errors). This plan is prepared for execution when ready.

---

## Technical Overview & Objectives

1. **WebSocket Protocol Migration**:
   - Replace HTTP POST registration endpoints on the wearable with real-time bidirectional WebSocket message frames.
   - Client sends JSON frame: `{"type": "register", "name": "...", "driveLink": "..."}`.
   - Wearable responds via WS broadcast/unicast frame: `{"type": "register_result", "success": true, "token": "RAMS-9921"}`.

2. **Unified Dark Slate Aesthetic & Zero-Emoji Rule**:
   - Maintain the dark slate monochromatic design (`#060913` base, `#0e1230` card surface, `#27272a` borders).
   - Use high-contrast monospaced uppercase controls and inline SVG vector icons instead of emojis.
   - Include the official system logo in top-left header.

